{# A library item chosen in a modal rather than in a <select> - the trigger half of the pattern, the
   other being templates/_library_picker.html.twig.

   **The select is still the field.** It stays in the form, keeps its name, its choices and its
   server-side rule; it is merely not what the teacher reads any more, because a library of two
   hundred quizzes is not a list one scrolls. The modal writes into it and fires a `change`, so every
   controller already listening on it (quiz-pool, quiz-launch) goes on working untouched.

   Parameters: `field` the form child, `placeholder` what the button says while nothing is chosen,
   `select_attr` the attributes the select must keep (its targets and actions).

   A screen with no Symfony form at all - Outils > Concours live - `embed`s this template instead and
   overrides the `select` block with its own `<select>`. The wrapper, the button and the contract
   with library_picker_controller.js stay written once. #}
{% set placeholder = placeholder|default('libraryPickerChooseAction'|trans) %}
<div class="cm-pickfield" data-picker-field data-picker-placeholder="{{ placeholder }}">
    {% block select %}{{ form_widget(field, {attr: {class: 'cm-pickfield__select'}|merge(select_attr|default({}))}) }}{% endblock %}
    <button type="button" class="cm-pickfield__button" data-action="library-picker#open">
        <span class="cm-pickfield__ico" aria-hidden="true">
            {# The item's own glyph, not a folder's: what the button holds once filled is one thing
               taken out of the library, and the tree is where the folders are drawn. #}
            <twig:ux:icon name="file-text" width="16" height="16"/>
        </span>
        <span class="cm-pickfield__label" data-picker-label>{{ placeholder }}</span>
        <span class="cm-pickfield__action">{{ 'libraryPickerBrowseAction'|trans }}</span>
    </button>
</div>
